import java.util.ArrayList;

// Define ValueKnapsack class inheriting from Knapsack
public class ValueKnapsack extends Knapsack {
    private ArrayList<Integer> itemValues; // List to store the value of items

    // Constructor for ValueKnapsack, initializes capacity and itemValues list
    public ValueKnapsack(int weightCapacity) {
        super(weightCapacity); // Call the constructor of the parent class
        itemValues = new ArrayList<Integer>(); // Initialize the itemValues list
    }

    // Method to add an item with name, weight and value
    public void addItem(String name, int weight, int value) {
        super.addItem(name, weight); // Add item to parent class lists
        itemValues.add(value); // Add the item value to the itemValues list
    }

    // Method to remove an item by name
    public void removeItem(String name) {
        int itemIndex = itemNames.indexOf(name); // Find index of the item name
        if (itemIndex >= 0) { // Check if item exists in the list
            super.removeItem(name); // Remove item from parent class lists
            itemValues.remove(itemIndex); // Remove the item value from itemValues list
        }
    }

    // Method to get the total value of items in the knapsack
    public int getTotalValue() {
        int totalValue = 0; // Initialize total value counter
        for (int value : itemValues) { // Iterate over all item values
            totalValue += value; // Accumulate value
        }
        return totalValue; // Return total value
    }
}
```

- **Inheritance**: `ValueKnapsack` extends `Knapsack` to effectively reuse and extend the functionality while adhering to object-oriented principles.
- **New Instance Variable**: `itemValues` is introduced to track the values associated with each item.
- **Constructor**: The constructor calls the superclass (Knapsack) constructor and initializes the new `itemValues` list.
- **Method Overriding**: 
  - `addItem` is overridden to handle the additional value parameter and store it in `itemValues`.
  - `removeItem` is overridden to ensure the corresponding value is also removed along with the item name and weight.
- **New Method**: `getTotalValue` calculates and returns the total value of all items currently in the knapsack.
